      <description>The Romagnola cattle breed has the inherent quality to increase beef production in South Africa markedly, according to Marnus Lessing, owner of the JML Romagnola stud near Lindley in the Free State, who succeeded in pushing up weaner weights considerably through crossbreeding Romagnolas with Brahmans.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.farmersweekly.co.za/animals/cattle/romagnola-beef-cattle-vastly-increased-weaner-weights-on-a-free-state-farm/#utm_source=rss&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=romagnola-beef-cattle-vastly-increased-weaner-weights-on-a-free-state-farm</guid>
